WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.389
In the last video we plugged the 144-fiber
trunk into the top of rack switch.

2
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:11.571
Now we follow it to the other end.

3
00:00:12.921 --> 00:00:20.897
We will look at the end of row rack, its big
panel, the front where the trunks from the TPU

4
00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:28.522
racks land, the back where 192-fiber trunks
leave, how the two sides line up, and where

5
00:00:28.522 --> 00:00:29.924
those trunks go.

6
00:00:34.074 --> 00:00:37.018
The rack at the end of your row has two names.

7
00:00:37.768 --> 00:00:40.115
End of row, or EOR.

8
00:00:40.865 --> 00:00:43.190
And all-in-one, or AIO.

9
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.625
It is the same rack.

10
00:00:47.925 --> 00:00:55.840
The most important part for this lesson is the
MPO four RU panel, at RU thirty-two.

11
00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:00.323
RU means rack unit, one slot of the rack.

12
00:01:02.623 --> 00:01:06.634
The trunks from the TPU racks land on its
front.

13
00:01:07.384 --> 00:01:11.501
The 192-fiber trunks leave from its back.

14
00:01:12.851 --> 00:01:21.234
You will also see copper panels at RU thirty,
twenty-four and twenty-two, and an LC panel at

15
00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.601
RU thirty-nine.

16
00:01:23.351 --> 00:01:26.039
Those are lessons twelve and thirteen.

17
00:01:27.389 --> 00:01:29.607
The switches are pre-installed.

18
00:01:30.357 --> 00:01:33.429
And note: this drawing is not to scale.

19
00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:38.979
Go by the checked RU numbers and the rack
integration spec.

20
00:01:43.129 --> 00:01:45.604
Here is that panel from the front.

21
00:01:46.354 --> 00:01:52.818
It has twelve rows, numbered from the bottom,
row one, up to row twelve at the top.

22
00:01:54.168 --> 00:01:56.493
And twelve columns, A to L.

23
00:01:57.243 --> 00:02:02.513
Each column has two ports, so each row has
twenty-four ports.

24
00:02:03.863 --> 00:02:09.729
Each port is pre-labeled with its column, its
port number, and its row.

25
00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:16.282
The first port here is A1 dash 1: column A,
port one, row one.

26
00:02:17.632 --> 00:02:22.048
Rule one for the front: one TPU rack per row.

27
00:02:22.798 --> 00:02:27.150
The lowest numbered TPU rack goes on the
bottom row.

28
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:36.665
Rows ten, eleven and twelve are reserved as
spares, and columns J, K and L are left open

29
00:02:36.665 --> 00:02:38.057
for the future.

30
00:02:42.207 --> 00:02:43.487
Now the legs.

31
00:02:44.237 --> 00:02:47.864
They go left to right, lowest number on the
left.

32
00:02:49.064 --> 00:02:51.603
Legs one and two go in column A.

33
00:02:52.953 --> 00:02:55.491
Legs three and four in column B.

34
00:02:56.241 --> 00:02:58.609
Five and six in column C.

35
00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:04.823
And so on, until legs fifteen and sixteen in
column H.

36
00:03:06.173 --> 00:03:10.867
Legs seventeen and eighteen, the spares, go in
column I.

37
00:03:12.217 --> 00:03:19.043
So the third TPU rack's leg five would go in
column C, port five, row three.

38
00:03:19.793 --> 00:03:22.161
Label C5 dash 3.

39
00:03:23.511 --> 00:03:24.642
One note.

40
00:03:25.392 --> 00:03:35.862
For end of row rack 511, which serves racks
502 to 510, this rule puts 502 on row one and

41
00:03:35.862 --> 00:03:37.744
510 on row nine.

42
00:03:38.494 --> 00:03:40.435
Confirm on your cutsheet.

43
00:03:44.585 --> 00:03:47.231
Now walk around to the back of the rack.

44
00:03:47.981 --> 00:03:49.666
Everything is mirrored.

45
00:03:50.416 --> 00:03:53.744
Facing the rear, column A is on the right.

46
00:03:54.494 --> 00:03:56.286
You work right to left.

47
00:03:57.786 --> 00:04:02.351
Each 192-fiber trunk takes one column.

48
00:04:03.101 --> 00:04:06.664
Column A goes to DCN patch panel one.

49
00:04:07.414 --> 00:04:10.123
Column B to patch panel two.

50
00:04:10.873 --> 00:04:14.031
Up to column H, patch panel eight.

51
00:04:15.381 --> 00:04:20.949
So every end of row rack sends eight 192-fiber
trunks.

52
00:04:22.299 --> 00:04:26.757
The trunk's twenty-four legs go up the column,
two per row.

53
00:04:27.507 --> 00:04:34.439
Legs one and two in row one, all the way to
legs twenty-three and twenty-four in row

54
00:04:34.439 --> 00:04:35.017
twelve.

55
00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:43.129
Odd legs go on the right port, even legs on
the left port, as seen from the rear.

56
00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:51.071
Legs nineteen to twenty-four, the top three
rows, are spares to the patch panel.

57
00:04:55.221 --> 00:04:57.163
Here is the key idea.

58
00:04:57.913 --> 00:05:00.558
Each port goes straight through the panel.

59
00:05:01.308 --> 00:05:05.489
The front of a port and the back of the same
port are joined.

60
00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:16.497
So TPU rack three, on front row three, meets
every 192-fiber trunk in rear row three.

61
00:05:17.847 --> 00:05:20.834
Its legs one and two sit in column A.

62
00:05:21.584 --> 00:05:26.917
Behind them is the column A trunk, which goes
to patch panel one.

63
00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:33.750
Its legs three and four sit in column B, so
they go to patch panel two.

64
00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:40.967
And its legs fifteen and sixteen, in column H,
go to patch panel eight.

65
00:05:42.317 --> 00:05:45.111
That is true for every TPU rack.

66
00:05:45.861 --> 00:05:50.960
Legs one and two of every rack go to patch
panel one, and so on.

67
00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:56.555
And this is why the rear view puts odd legs on
the right.

68
00:05:57.305 --> 00:06:01.273
From the front, the first port of a column is
on the left.

69
00:06:02.023 --> 00:06:05.543
From behind, that same port is on the right.

70
00:06:06.293 --> 00:06:09.109
The odd legs land right behind it.

71
00:06:13.259 --> 00:06:16.225
Which rack does each column's trunk go to?

72
00:06:16.975 --> 00:06:20.601
The trunk landing sheet in the guide answers
that.

73
00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:28.799
End of row racks at spot eleven, on the north
side, land in the north rack of each pair.

74
00:06:29.549 --> 00:06:33.197
Racks at spot thirteen land in the south rack.

75
00:06:34.547 --> 00:06:39.773
So column A from a spot eleven rack goes to
rack 107.

76
00:06:40.523 --> 00:06:44.449
From a spot thirteen rack, it goes to 108.

77
00:06:45.799 --> 00:06:50.407
And column H goes to 227 or 228.

78
00:06:51.757 --> 00:06:58.712
The guide numbers these patch panels one to
eight in one place, and letters them A to H in

79
00:06:58.712 --> 00:06:59.330
another.

80
00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.003
Patch panel one is patch panel A.

81
00:07:07.153 --> 00:07:15.354
In lesson eight of the course, you will pick
front ports for TPU legs, and work out where

82
00:07:15.354 --> 00:07:20.699
192-fiber legs land and which patch panel rack
they go to.

